--For cases where you need responsive decimal places.  For example 1,234,456.0000 should become 1,234,456 and 0 should become 0.0123

--Step 1.  Turn your numeric column into a measure:
Result_numeric_measure= SELECTEDVALUE(Table[Result_numeric])

--Step 2. Use your measure where you'd use the regular field
-- Click on the measure in the data panel
-- Go to 'Measure tools'
-- In the Format box, select 'dynamic' from the drop down
-- To the left of the formula bar, and to the left of the green tick/red cross, you can select 'Measure' or 'Format'.
-- Select 'Format'
-- In the formula bar, paste this:

IF (
    SELECTEDMEASURE() <= 1,
    "#,##0.00",
    "#,##0"
)

-- This code gives all values <=1 two decimal places, else no decimal places.  
-- Alter this to suit your needs
-- You can also include string values where needed into the formula.  
